  "case_id": "CASE-2026-006",
  "label": "drift",
  "narrative": "No single transaction ever breaches the ₾600 per-transaction cap, and the ₾8,000 monthly cap is never technically breached either (June ₾1,820 → July ₾4,931 → August ₾6,958 — trending toward it, not over it). What breaks is the baseline: over June's first four weeks the agent runs a tight pattern (avg ₾182/tx, 3/week, four established fuel/logistics vendors, almost entirely MCC 5541). From week 5 onward, average transaction size climbs steadily to ~₾370, weekly frequency rises to 6, a vendor never used in the baseline period (Batumi Express Freight) grows to account for most transactions, and a new category (vehicle maintenance, MCC 7538, via a second new vendor) enters the mix. No rule catches any one of these; the trend across ~11 weeks is the finding.",
